These additive support-aware localization kernels include the unchanged
independent native implementation in ../ssg-full/localization.cpp. Keep that
implementation's credits and license, and the PocketFFT license, with this
dependency. The word and phrase definitions credit Wang et al., TIFS 18 (2023),
DOI 10.1109/TIFS.2023.3234861 and the original word2phraseCMFD method.

The separate original structured-forest model and detector retain their MSR-LA
noncommercial terms; the Piotr channel implementation retains its BSD notice.
This adapter does not relicense those resources or modify the forest weights.

Added 2026-10-21: explicit observed-support Gaussian/SSIM and scalar morphology,
candidate-domain components and hole filling. The complete-rectangle paths use
the unchanged native kernels. Source-region context boundaries and support
adaptations are reported separately from algorithm parameters.
